# Internal process packs and their qualification evidence.
# These are working material for a single machine: they carry local paths,
# candidate SHAs and internal review records, and this repository is public.
MARSHAL_PROCESS_*/
MARSHAL_TUI_ULTIMATE_SPEC/
MARSHAL-*-MEGA-TASK/

# Task specification packs. These are working documents handed to an agent, not
# part of MARSHAL, and some of them name the production host, its paths and its
# admin ports. Ignoring them here means a `git add -A` cannot sweep that into a
# public repository by accident — which it very nearly did.
MARSHAL_COMMUNITY_CLOUD_ULTRA_ACTIVATION_TELEMETRY_FINAL_MEGA_ULTRA_V2/

# Cross-agent briefing targets. MARSHAL's project-doc injection channel writes a
# generated block into these, quoting other agents' sessions and tool output —
# which can include internal architecture it happened to read. They are local
# context handed to a CLI, not part of MARSHAL, so `git add -A` must not sweep
# them into a public repository. AGENTS.example.md stays tracked.
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md

# Local working material that describes the project's internals: specification
# drafts, architecture trees, audit reports and qualification evidence handed to
# an agent. This repository is public, so everything of that kind is collected
# here and kept out of it. Nothing MARSHAL ships at runtime belongs in secrets/.
/secrets/
